   "value": "## The precise untwisting relation\n\nNotation: $V_\\lambda(z)=\\prod_{i<j}(z_i-z_j)^{\\lambda_i-\\lambda_j}$; rows $(\\alpha,i,j)$, $\\alpha\\in\\{1,2\\}$, $(i,j)\\in\\{(1,3),(1,2),(2,3)\\}$; columns in the integral-of-motion basis $H=(c_1+c_3,\\,c_5-c_6+5c_3,\\,c_2-c_3)$, $O=(c_4,\\,c_6+c_3,\\,c_3)$. Q-functions regularized to the monic untwisted staggered ones ($Q_1$, $Q^3$ raw; $Q_2\\to q_2$, $Q^2\\to q^2$).\n\n**1. Laplace split (Appendix N).** The bare rows $\\alpha=1$ vanish, and only one Laplace term survives:\n$$\n\\det N_{\\rm reg}=-\\det\\big[A_1\\big]_{O}\\;\\det\\big[A_2\\big]_{H}\\,\\big(1+O(\\varepsilon)\\big).\n$$\n\n**2. Periodic block.** $\\det[A_2]_H\\to\\det[A_2]_H^{\\rm untw}$: the $3\\times3$ minor of **untwisted** Q-functions, periodic measure $e^{2\\pi iu/h}$, $H$ columns.\n\n**3. Bare block, from the residue at infinity.**\n$$\n\\det\\big[A_1\\big]_{O}=V_{\\lambda}(z)\\,E_\\lambda\\,(1+O(\\varepsilon)),\\qquad\nE_\\lambda=-\\frac{(\\lambda_1-\\lambda_2+1)(\\lambda_2-\\lambda_3+1)}{(\\lambda_1-\\lambda_3+1)!\\,(\\lambda_1-\\lambda_2)!\\,(\\lambda_2-\\lambda_3)!},\n$$\nwhere $\\lambda$ is the total highest weight. The three factorials are $(5-d_{ij})!$ with $d_{ij}=\\deg q_i+\\deg q^j$, as in (N3)–(N4). The numerator is the product of the leading coefficients of the untwisted Casoratians $q_1\\wedge q_2$ and $q^3\\wedge q^2$.\n\n**4. Normalization factors.** $c^{\\rm ref}_{\\rm reg}\\Psi^{\\rm ref}_{\\rm reg}\\to(c\\Psi)^{\\rm untw}$, and hence $C_{\\rm vac}=\\dfrac{(c\\Psi)^{\\rm untw}_{\\rm vac}}{V_{\\lambda_{\\rm vac}}(z)\\,E_{\\lambda_{\\rm vac}}\\det[A_2]^{\\rm untw}_{H,\\rm vac}}\\,(1+O(\\varepsilon))$.\n\n**Result.**\n$$\n\\boxed{\\;\\lim_{\\varepsilon\\to0}\\;\\frac{V_{\\lambda_{\\rm vac}}(z)}{V_{\\lambda_A}(z)}\\,\n\\frac{\\langle L_A|R_A\\rangle}{\\langle L_A|0\\rangle\\langle0|R_A\\rangle}\n=\\frac{E_{\\lambda_A}\\,\\det[A_2]^{\\rm untw}_{H,A}\\,/\\,(c^{\\rm ref}\\Psi^{\\rm ref})^{\\rm untw}_A}\n{E_{\\lambda_{\\rm vac}}\\,\\det[A_2]^{\\rm untw}_{H,\\rm vac}\\,/\\,(c^{\\rm ref}\\Psi^{\\rm ref})^{\\rm untw}_{\\rm vac}}\\;}\n$$\nEverything on the right is built from untwisted Q-functions and explicit numbers.\n\n**Evidence.**\n- Chain point $\\theta=(1/3,-8/57)$: split residual $O(\\varepsilon)$; $E$ matches its numerical value to $10^{-18}$; the boxed ratio matches the physical limit to $10^{-19}$; three twist directions.\n- **Independent** chain point $\\theta=(1/5,46/55)$, $\\varphi=(3/2,1/2,-2)$ (cell 10): split residual $\\sim10^{-7}$ at $\\varepsilon=10^{-8}$; $E_\\lambda$ formula to $10^{-13}$–$10^{-14}$ for all six states.\n\nThe formula for $E_\\lambda$ was identified from the first chain point (four degree patterns) and then **independently validated** at the second. It has not been derived analytically yet: the $\\alpha=1$, $O$ block has a leading-order degeneracy ($O_1+O_2$ cancels), so the derivation needs the next order of the residue-at-infinity expansion.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## Matching to bare untwisted eigenvectors\n\nThe GT generators satisfy $E_{ji}=S^{-1}E_{ij}^{T}S$ with $S={\\rm diag}(1,1,1,2,6,9,4,9)$ per site. So the left highest-weight covector is $l_0\\propto(S\\otimes S)\\,r_0$, and the natural bilinear norm is $\\|r_0\\|^2_S=r_0^T(S\\otimes S)r_0$. The question is which normalization $\\mathcal N(r_0)$ gives $\\|r_0\\|^2_S/\\mathcal N(r_0)^2=\\mathcal B_{\\lambda_A}/\\mathcal B_{\\lambda_{\\rm vac}}$. To see the $\\theta$-dependence, the explicit Q-formula is evaluated at $\\theta=(t,0)$ for several rational $t$, chosen from $t=(m-1)(m-5)/(m^2-5)$ so that the octets are rational too.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- 11. Explicit Q-formula and exact untwisted eigenvectors at theta = (t, 0). ---- *)\nClearAll[Sdiag, S2U, buildAtU, bracketExplU, BexplU, dataAtU, tValsU];\n\nSdiag = {1, 1, 1, 2, 6, 9, 4, 9};\nS2U = Flatten[KroneckerProduct[Sdiag, Sdiag]];\n\n(* Rebuild the untwisted chain and states at theta = {t, 0}. *)\nbuildAtU[t_] := (\n   thetaU = {t, 0};\n   Do[With[{m = qminorU[II]},\n     Do[qcoU[II, k] = Coefficient[m, u, k], {k, 0, 2 Length[II]}]],\n    {II, Join @@ (Subsets[Range[3], {#}] & /@ Range[3])}];\n   untwU = Module[{recs},\n     recs = Flatten[Table[Module[{Bt = hwBasisU[w], r, Rk, evs, ev, p},\n         r = First@Select[Subsets[Range[dcU], {Length[Bt[[1]]]}], Det[Bt[[#]]] =!= 0 &, 1];\n         Rk[a_, k_] := Inverse[Bt[[r]]].(TcoU[a, k, {1, 1, 1}].Bt)[[r]];\n         evs = Eigenvectors[Rk[2, 0]];\n         Table[ev = evs[[c]]; p = First@Flatten@Position[Unitize[ev], 1];\n          <|\"mu\" -> w, \"vec\" -> Bt.ev,\n            \"T1\" -> Sum[(Rk[1, k].ev)[[p]]/ev[[p]] u^k, {k, 0, 2}],\n            \"T2\" -> Sum[(Rk[2, k].ev)[[p]]/ev[[p]] u^k, {k, 0, 4}]|>, {c, Length[evs]}]],\n        {w, hwMusU}], 1];\n     recs = SortBy[recs, {First@Flatten@Position[hwMusU, #[\"mu\"]] &, Coefficient[#[\"T2\"], u, 0] &}];\n     Table[Append[s, <|\"q\" -> polyKernelU[BaxDirU[s[\"T1\"], s[\"T2\"], 1]],\n        \"qd\" -> Reverse[polyKernelU[BaxDualU[s[\"T1\"], s[\"T2\"], 1]]]|>], {s, recs}]]);\n\n(* The explicit formula of the tex note, independent of the twisted machinery. *)\nbracketExplU[f_] := With[{poles = Flatten@Table[th + n, {th, thetaU}, {n, 0, 2}]},\n   Sum[Exp[2 Pi I SetPrecision[p, 80]] f[p]/Times @@ (p - DeleteCases[poles, p]), {p, poles}]];\nBexplU[s_] := Module[{q, qd, lam = s[\"mu\"], Nm, psi, cref},\n   q = Function[{i, x}, qpolyU[s[\"q\"][[i]], x]];\n   qd = Function[{j, x}, qpolyU[s[\"qd\"][[j]], x]];\n   Nm = Table[{\n      bracketExplU[Function[x, qd[ij[[2]], x + 1] q[ij[[1]], x] - qd[ij[[2]], x] q[ij[[1]], x]]],\n      bracketExplU[Function[x, x qd[ij[[2]], x] q[ij[[1]], x - 1] - (x - 5) qd[ij[[2]], x + 1] q[ij[[1]], x]]],\n      bracketExplU[Function[x, qd[ij[[2]], x] q[ij[[1]], x - 1] - qd[ij[[2]], x + 1] q[ij[[1]], x]]]},\n     {ij, {{1, 3}, {1, 2}, {2, 3}}}];\n   psi = Product[q[1, th + 1] (q[1, th] q[2, th - 1] - q[2, th] q[1, th - 1]), {th, thetaU}];\n   cref = Product[(qd[3, th + 1] (qd[3, th] qd[2, th + 1] - qd[2, th] qd[3, th + 1])\n       - qd[3, th] (qd[3, th] qd[2, th + 2] - qd[2, th] qd[3, th + 2]))/4, {th, thetaU}];\n   EformulaU[lam] Det[Nm]/(cref psi)];\n\ntValsU = {9/19, -3/11, 5/31, 3/11, 21/59, 8/19};\ndataAtU = Table[(buildAtU[t];\n    With[{bs = BexplU /@ untwU},\n     {t, Table[{untwU[[m, \"mu\"]], Rationalize[Chop[bs[[m]]/bs[[1]], 10^-50], 10^-40],\n        untwU[[m, \"vec\"]], untwU[[m, \"vec\"]].(S2U untwU[[m, \"vec\"]])}, {m, 6}]}]),\n   {t, tValsU}];\n\nGrid[Prepend[Table[{d[[1]], Sequence @@ d[[2, All, 2]]}, {d, dataAtU}],\n   {\"t\", \"B/B_vac: 27\", \"10\", \"10b\", \"8_1\", \"8_2\", \"1\"}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
